    "report": "Messaging and Notifications no longer read the machine's clock. Every time they decide or record now comes from the application's clock (machine time plus `CLOCK_OFFSET_DAYS`), passed in from the wiring. The work is committed on `main` as `3f13e43` and not pushed. I didn't start a server.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Messaging domain:** `Conversation.start`, `send` and `report` take their time as a required parameter. The `new Date()` defaults are gone, including the one that stamped a message when `sentAt` was omitted.\n- **Messaging handlers and wiring:** `StartConversation`, `SendMessage` and `ReportMessage` take the clock as a required constructor argument. `messagingWiring` requires it too. `ReportMessage` had no clock before, so I added one.\n- **Notifications domain:** `NoticeWindow.admit`, `MessageNoticeOwing.owe` and `Notice.accept` take a required time.\n- **Notifications application:** `MessageSentIntegrationEventHandler` and `NoticeDelivery` receive the clock. `notificationsWiring` takes it, and `createApplication` passes the clock it already builds.\n- **Specs:** the specs that relied on the defaults pass a fixed instant (`2026-11-16T10:00:00Z`) instead.\n\n**Checks**\n- `yarn typecheck`: passes.\n- `yarn check:conventions`: passes.\n- ESLint and Prettier on the changed files: pass.\n- Unit tests for Messaging and Notifications: 15 suites, 72 tests pass.\n- Messaging, Notifications and message-clock end-to-end specs: 22 suites, 103 tests pass. The one `Connection terminated` log is a background notice delivery running as the test database closes. It is noise, not a failure.\n- I did not run the full end-to-end suite across every context.\n\n**Decisions I made**\n- **Branch:** the harness guidance says to branch off a default branch before committing. You asked for the current branch, so I committed on `main`.\n- **Clock parameter order:** `notificationsWiring` now takes the clock before `notifyUrl`, so its callers' positional arguments changed. Only `createApplication` calls it.\n- **Test instant:** I used a fixed instant in specs rather than `new Date()`, so the specs don't read the machine's clock either.\n\n**Unclear, not changed**\n- Notifications' calendar-conflict and email-verification owing have no time parameters and read no clock, so I left them alone. They fall under the \"a time is given, never defaulted\" rule only if they ever start deciding on time.",
